        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "## Part 2 - Load open data into the database",
          "",
          "The **Unfallatlas** of the statistical offices lists every road accident with personal injury in Germany, with its location. You read the original files directly from Object Storage, keep the accidents of Nuremberg, and store them in a spatial table.",
          "",
          "About the files:",
          "* Semicolon as separator, one file per year, all of Germany.",
          "* Some files start with a byte order mark (BOM). `encoding='utf-8-sig'` removes it.",
          "* The column names differ slightly between years. 2020 calls the road condition `STRZUSTAND`, later years `IstStrassenzustand`.",
          "* `LINREFX`, `LINREFY` are coordinates in ETRS89 / UTM zone 32N (EPSG:25832).",
          "* Codes, e.g. `UKATEGORIE`: 1 = killed, 2 = seriously injured, 3 = slightly injured. `IstRad` = 1: a bicycle was involved."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Read the accident files and keep the Nuremberg accidents",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "frames = []",
          "for year, file_name in ACCIDENT_FILES.items():",
          "    df = pd.read_csv(PAR_URL + DATA_PREFIX + file_name, sep=';', dtype=str, encoding='utf-8-sig')",
          "    df = df.rename(columns={'STRZUSTAND': 'IstStrassenzustand'})          # 2020 uses the old name",
          "    ags = df['ULAND'] + df['UREGBEZ'] + df['UKREIS'] + df['UGEMEINDE']    # 8-digit municipality key",
          "    df = df[ags.str.startswith(REGION_AGS)].copy()",
          "    df['AGS'] = ags[df.index]",
          "    print(f'{year}: {len(df):>6,} accidents in region {REGION_AGS}, {int((df[\"IstRad\"] == \"1\").sum()):>4} with a bicycle')",
          "    frames.append(df)",
          "",
          "raw = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True)",
          "print(f'\\nTotal: {len(raw):,} accidents')"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "raw",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Expected result",
          "```",
          "2020:  1,755 accidents in region 09564000,  741 with a bicycle",
          "2021:  1,792 accidents in region 09564000,  732 with a bicycle",
          "2022:  1,926 accidents in region 09564000,  801 with a bicycle",
          "2023:  1,868 accidents in region 09564000,  729 with a bicycle",
          "2024:  1,915 accidents in region 09564000,  709 with a bicycle",
          "2025:  1,746 accidents in region 09564000,  675 with a bicycle",
          "",
          "Total: 11,002 accidents",
          "```",
          "Each file holds all accidents with personal injury in Germany for one year, about 240,000 to 270,000 rows. The municipality key keeps only Nuremberg. In Nuremberg, a bicycle is involved in about 40 % of these accidents. The paragraph downloads six files of about 40 MB each, so it can take a minute."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
