      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Accidents per year in the database",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%sql",
          "",
          "SELECT acc_year,",
          "       COUNT(*)                                     AS accidents,",
          "       SUM(is_bicycle)                              AS with_bicycle,",
          "       SUM(CASE WHEN is_bicycle = 1 AND category <= 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS bicycle_killed_or_serious",
          "FROM   nue_accidents",
          "GROUP  BY acc_year",
          "ORDER  BY acc_year"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "table",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Expected result",
          "",
          "```",
          "ACC_YEAR  ACCIDENTS  WITH_BICYCLE  BICYCLE_KILLED_OR_SERIOUS",
          "--------  ---------  ------------  -------------------------",
          "    2020       1755           741                        143",
          "    2021       1792           732                        126",
          "    2022       1926           801                        135",
          "    2023       1868           729                        125",
          "    2024       1915           709                         89",
          "    2025       1746           675                        100",
          "```",
          "",
          "This SQL runs directly on the new table. The numbers are the same as in the Python output above, so nothing was lost on the way into the database. In 2020-2023, 17-19 % of the bicycle accidents killed or seriously injured someone, in 2024 and 2025 13-15 %."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
