      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "The **Zensus 2022** counted the residents of Germany in 100 m grid cells, by age group. The workshop uses the Bavarian part of the file for all of Germany: the same columns, but only the cells in Bavaria. You read it in pieces of 500,000 rows and keep only the cells around Nuremberg. Each cell becomes a 100 m square.",
          "",
          "About the file:",
          "* Columns: `Insgesamt_Bevoelkerung` (residents), `Unter18`, `a18bis29`, `a30bis49`, `a50bis64`, `a65undaelter`.",
          "* `x_mp_100m`, `y_mp_100m` are the cell midpoints in ETRS89 / LAEA Europe (EPSG:3035), the coordinate system of all European statistical grids.",
          "* To protect privacy, small numbers are suppressed and shown as `–`. They become empty values (NULL). The number of residents is never suppressed."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Read the Zensus 2022 grid and keep the cells around Nuremberg",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "# Area of interest: all Nuremberg accidents plus 1 km, in the coordinate system of the census grid",
          "xmin, ymin, xmax, ymax = acc_gdf.to_crs(CRS_CENSUS).total_bounds",
          "xmin, ymin, xmax, ymax = xmin - 1000, ymin - 1000, xmax + 1000, ymax + 1000",
          "",
          "CENSUS_COLUMNS = {'GITTER_ID_100m': 'GRID_ID', 'Insgesamt_Bevoelkerung': 'POPULATION', 'Unter18': 'UNDER_18',",
          "                  'a18bis29': 'AGE_18_29', 'a30bis49': 'AGE_30_49', 'a50bis64': 'AGE_50_64', 'a65undaelter': 'AGE_65_PLUS'}",
          "parts = []",
          "for chunk in pd.read_csv(PAR_URL + DATA_PREFIX + CENSUS_FILE, sep=';', na_values=['–'], chunksize=500_000,",
          "                         usecols=list(CENSUS_COLUMNS) + ['x_mp_100m', 'y_mp_100m']):",
          "    inside = chunk['x_mp_100m'].between(xmin, xmax) & chunk['y_mp_100m'].between(ymin, ymax)",
          "    parts.append(chunk[inside])",
          "cen = pd.concat(parts, ignore_index=True)",
          "",
          "squares = [box(x - 50, y - 50, x + 50, y + 50) for x, y in zip(cen['x_mp_100m'], cen['y_mp_100m'])]",
          "census_gdf = gpd.GeoDataFrame(cen.rename(columns=CENSUS_COLUMNS).drop(columns=['x_mp_100m', 'y_mp_100m']),",
          "                              geometry=squares, crs=CRS_CENSUS)",
          "print(f'Grid cells around Nuremberg: {len(census_gdf):,}   residents: {int(census_gdf[\"POPULATION\"].sum()):,}')"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "raw",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Expected result",
          "```",
          "Grid cells around Nuremberg: 11,780   residents: 727,193",
          "```",
          "The file covers Bavaria, about 565,000 grid cells. Only the cells in a rectangle around the Nuremberg accidents are kept. The rectangle also includes neighbouring towns such as Fürth, which is why there are more residents than Nuremberg's about 530,000. Only the cells inside the hexagons count later. The paragraph downloads about 37 MB."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Write the census grid to table NUE_CENSUS_GRID",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "write(census_gdf.to_crs(CRS_STORE), DBSpatialDataset(table=T_CENSUS), if_exists='replace', create_spatial_index=True)",
          "print(f'Table {T_CENSUS}: {len(census_gdf):,} rows written, spatial index created.')",
          "del cen, parts, squares"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "raw",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
