        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "## Part 3 - Explore bicycle accidents: types, time and place",
          "",
          "A `SpatialDataFrame` works like a GeoPandas data frame, but it references the table in the database. Filters, spatial operations such as *nearest neighbours* or *within distance*, and measurements run in Oracle Spatial."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Create SpatialDataFrames for the accidents and the cycling infrastructure",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "acc_sdf   = SpatialDataFrame.create(DBSpatialDataset(table=T_ACCIDENTS))",
          "infra_sdf = SpatialDataFrame.create(DBSpatialDataset(table=T_INFRA))",
          "",
          "# Only accidents with a bicycle involved",
          "bike_sdf = acc_sdf[acc_sdf['IS_BICYCLE'] == 1]",
          "print(f'All accidents: {acc_sdf.shape[0]:,}   with a bicycle: {bike_sdf.shape[0]:,}   cycling ways: {infra_sdf.shape[0]:,}')",
          "z.show(bike_sdf.head())"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "table",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Expected result",
          "```",
          "All accidents: 11,002   with a bicycle: 4,387   cycling ways: 3,638",
          "```",
          "followed by a table of five bicycle accidents, all with `IS_BICYCLE` = 1. Which five rows you see can differ, because the database does not return rows in a fixed order.",
          "",
          "A `SpatialDataFrame` does not copy the data into Python. It references the table, and the filter `acc_sdf['IS_BICYCLE'] == 1` creates another reference with a condition."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Map of bicycle accidents and cycling infrastructure",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "_, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 12))",
          "infra_sdf.to_crs(CRS_METRIC).plot(ax=ax, color='#2c7fb8', linewidth=0.8, with_basemap=True)",
          "bike_sdf.to_crs(CRS_METRIC).plot(ax=ax, color='#d7301f', markersize=3, alpha=0.5, with_basemap=True)",
          "ax.set_title('Bicycle accidents (red) and cycling infrastructure (blue), Nuremberg')",
          "ax.set_axis_off()"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
