      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "## Part 4 - Find accident clusters with DBSCAN",
          "",
          "**In one sentence:** DBSCAN finds the places where accidents are packed closely together, and leaves single accidents alone.",
          "",
          "###### How DBSCAN works",
          "",
          "Imagine you stand on the map at an accident, draw a circle around you and count the accidents inside it. That is all DBSCAN does, for every accident:",
          "",
          "1. Around each accident, it draws a circle with the radius **eps** and counts the accidents inside.",
          "2. If there are at least **min_samples** accidents in the circle, the accident is a **core point**: the centre of a dense place.",
          "3. Core points whose circles overlap are joined into one **cluster**. Accidents inside the circle of a core point belong to that cluster too.",
          "4. All other accidents are **noise**: they are not part of a dense place.",
          "",
          "The name stands for *Density-Based Spatial Clustering of Applications with Noise*.",
          "",
          "###### Why DBSCAN fits this question",
          "",
          "* You do not have to say in advance how many clusters you expect, unlike k-means.",
          "* Clusters can have any shape: a crossing, a square or a stretch of road.",
          "* Single accidents are not forced into a cluster. Most accidents are noise, and that is fine.",
          "",
          "###### The two parameters",
          "",
          "* **eps = 50 m**: the radius of the circle, about the size of a large crossing.",
          "* **min_samples = 12**: at least 12 accidents within 50 m in six years, so about two per year at the same place.",
          "",
          "###### What DBSCAN cannot tell you",
          "",
          "A cluster shows where accidents are dense. It does not show whether that is unusual, because more accidents happen where more people cycle. Part 5 tests that.",
          "",
          "###### Coordinates in metres",
          "",
          "DBSCAN measures distances, so it needs projected coordinates in metres. The Spatial AI sample notebooks use Web Mercator (EPSG:3857). In Nuremberg, a \"metre\" in EPSG:3857 is only about 0.65 m on the ground. You therefore use UTM zone 32N (EPSG:25832), where 50 m are really 50 m."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Detect clusters of bicycle accidents",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "EPS_METRES  = 50",
          "MIN_SAMPLES = 12",
          "",
          "# Read the bicycle accidents once, in metres and in a fixed order (by ID),",
          "# so that the cluster labels match the rows later on",
          "bike_m = bike_sdf.to_crs(CRS_METRIC).as_geodataframe().sort_values('ID').reset_index(drop=True)",
          "X = SpatialDataFrame.create(GeoDataFrameDataset(bike_m[['geometry']]))",
          "coords = SCoordTransformer().transform(X)        # geometry -> x/y features",
          "",
          "dbscan = DBScanClustering(eps=EPS_METRES, min_samples=MIN_SAMPLES)",
          "labels = dbscan.fit_predict(coords)",
          "",
          "n_clusters = len(set(labels)) - (1 if -1 in labels else 0)",
          "print(f'Clusters: {n_clusters}')",
          "print(f'Accidents in clusters: {(labels >= 0).sum():,} of {len(labels):,} ({(labels >= 0).mean():.0%})')"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "raw",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
