      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "## Part 5 - Is it more than chance? Hotspot test",
          "",
          "Where many people cycle, there are more accidents. A cluster alone does not prove a problem. A **hotspot test** asks: *Is a place surrounded by places that also have many accidents, more than random variation would explain?*",
          "",
          "For that you need areas, not points. You cover the streets of Nuremberg with **hexagons** (150 m side length, about 6 hectares) and count the bicycle accidents in each one. Only hexagons within 150 m of any accident are kept, so that parks, forests and the airport do not distort the test.",
          "",
          "**Why hexagons?** Every hexagon has exactly six neighbours, they all share an edge with it, and their centres are all at the same distance. Squares have neighbours that only touch at a corner and are further away. So with hexagons, \"neighbour\" means the same everywhere.",
          "",
          "The test runs in three steps:",
          "1. **Spatial weights** define who the neighbours of each hexagon are.",
          "2. **Moran's I** checks the whole city: are busy hexagons next to busy hexagons?",
          "3. **LISA** checks each hexagon: where exactly are the hotspots?"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Create the hexagon grid and count bicycle accidents per hexagon",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "HEX_SIZE = 150    # side length in metres",
          "",
          "def hexagon_grid(bounds, size):",
          "    xmin, ymin, xmax, ymax = bounds",
          "    width, height = np.sqrt(3) * size, 1.5 * size",
          "    corners = np.radians(np.arange(30, 390, 60))",
          "    cells, row, y = [], 0, ymin",
          "    while y < ymax + height:",
          "        x = xmin + (width / 2 if row % 2 else 0)",
          "        while x < xmax + width:",
          "            cells.append(Polygon(zip(x + size * np.cos(corners), y + size * np.sin(corners))))",
          "            x += width",
          "        y += height",
          "        row += 1",
          "    return gpd.GeoDataFrame(geometry=cells, crs=CRS_METRIC)",
          "",
          "acc_m = acc_sdf.to_crs(CRS_METRIC).as_geodataframe()     # all accidents: where is traffic?",
          "",
          "grid = hexagon_grid(acc_m.total_bounds, HEX_SIZE)",
          "grid = grid[grid.intersects(acc_m.buffer(150).union_all())].reset_index(drop=True)",
          "grid.insert(0, 'CELL_ID', np.arange(1, len(grid) + 1))",
          "",
          "hits = gpd.sjoin(bike_m[['geometry']], grid, predicate='within')",
          "grid['BIKE_ACC'] = grid['CELL_ID'].map(hits['CELL_ID'].value_counts()).fillna(0).astype(int)",
          "",
          "grid_sdf = SpatialDataFrame.create(GeoDataFrameDataset(grid))",
          "print(f'Hexagons: {len(grid):,}   with at least one bicycle accident: {(grid[\"BIKE_ACC\"] > 0).sum():,}   maximum: {grid[\"BIKE_ACC\"].max()}')"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "raw",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Expected result",
          "```",
          "Hexagons: 2,646   with at least one bicycle accident: 1,165   maximum: 33",
          "```",
          "More than half of the hexagons have no bicycle accident at all. These zeros matter: the hotspot test compares busy places with quiet ones. The busiest hexagon had 33 bicycle accidents in six years."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
