      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Spatial weights: who are my neighbours?",
          "",
          "**In one sentence:** spatial weights are a list that says, for every hexagon, which hexagons are its neighbours.",
          "",
          "All spatial statistics and most Spatial AI methods compare a place with its surroundings. Before they can do that, they need to know what \"surroundings\" means. That is what spatial weights define.",
          "",
          "**How it works here:** `KNNWeightsDefinition(k=6)` takes the centre of every hexagon and finds the 6 nearest centres (k-nearest neighbours). In a hexagon grid, those are exactly the six hexagons around it. At the edge of the grid, some neighbours are a bit further away.",
          "",
          "**A graph:** together, the neighbour relations form a network. Every hexagon is a node, and every \"is a neighbour of\" is an edge. This is the graph behind the analysis: Moran's I and LISA move along these edges.",
          "",
          "**Other definitions:** Spatial AI also offers, for example, *Queen* (all areas that share an edge or a corner) and *distance band* (everything within a given distance). Which one fits depends on the data."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Create spatial weights and look at the neighbours of the busiest hexagon",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "knn6 = KNNWeightsDefinition(k=6)",
          "weights = SpatialWeights.create(grid_sdf, knn6)",
          "",
          "busiest = int(grid['BIKE_ACC'].idxmax())",
          "print(f'Busiest hexagon: CELL_ID {grid.loc[busiest, \"CELL_ID\"]} with {grid.loc[busiest, \"BIKE_ACC\"]} bicycle accidents')",
          "print('Its neighbours:', grid.iloc[weights.neighbors[busiest]][['CELL_ID', 'BIKE_ACC']].to_dict('records'))"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "raw",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Expected result",
          "```",
          "Busiest hexagon: CELL_ID 1543 with 33 bicycle accidents",
          "Its neighbours: [{'CELL_ID': 1542, 'BIKE_ACC': 12}, {'CELL_ID': 1587, 'BIKE_ACC': 13}, {'CELL_ID': 1586, 'BIKE_ACC': 10}, {'CELL_ID': 1544, 'BIKE_ACC': 14}, {'CELL_ID': 1503, 'BIKE_ACC': 7}, {'CELL_ID': 1502, 'BIKE_ACC': 15}]",
          "```",
          "The order of the neighbours can differ. The six neighbours of the busiest hexagon also have many accidents, between 7 and 15, while the average hexagon has fewer than 2. High values next to high values is exactly what Moran's I measures next."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
