          "The numbers can differ by a few hexagons between runs, because the p-values come from random permutations: a hexagon with a p-value close to 0.05 can be significant in one run and not in the next. About 8 % of the hexagons are hotspots, but they contain about 43 % of all bicycle accidents. The 31 HIGH-LOW hexagons stand out from a quiet neighbourhood."
        ],
