        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "## Part 8 - Where are there more bicycle accidents than expected?",
          "",
          "So far you counted accidents. But a busy street has more accidents simply because more people use it. A **regression model** estimates how many bicycle accidents a hexagon would have *given* what is there, and shows where reality is clearly worse.",
          "",
          "For each hexagon, the model uses three **explanatory variables**:",
          "",
          "```",
          "Variable                                              Stands for",
          "----------------------------------------------------  -----------------------------------------------------------------",
          "OTHER_ACC - accidents without a bicycle               how much road traffic there is (there are no open traffic counts)",
          "INFRA_100M - metres of cycling way / 100              how much cycling infrastructure there is",
          "YOUNG_100 - residents aged 18-29 / 100 (Zensus 2022)  how many people of the age group that cycles most live there",
          "```",
          "",
          "You compare two models:",
          "",
          "* **OLS** (ordinary least squares) finds **one rule for the whole city**, for example \"each accident without a bicycle comes with about 0.35 bicycle accidents\".",
          "* **GWR** (geographically weighted regression) finds **a separate rule for every hexagon**, using only its 150 nearest hexagons. It shows whether the rules differ between the centre and the outskirts."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Add the explanatory variables to every hexagon",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "# Residents aged 18-29: each census cell counts for the hexagon that contains its midpoint",
          "census_m = SpatialDataFrame.create(DBSpatialDataset(table=T_CENSUS)).to_crs(CRS_METRIC).as_geodataframe()",
          "census_pts = census_m[['POPULATION', 'AGE_18_29']].copy()",
          "census_pts = gpd.GeoDataFrame(census_pts, geometry=census_m.centroid, crs=CRS_METRIC)",
          "pop = gpd.sjoin(census_pts, grid[['CELL_ID', 'geometry']], predicate='within').groupby('CELL_ID')[['POPULATION', 'AGE_18_29']].sum()",
          "grid['POPULATION']   = grid['CELL_ID'].map(pop['POPULATION']).fillna(0).astype(int)",
          "grid['YOUNG_ADULTS'] = grid['CELL_ID'].map(pop['AGE_18_29']).fillna(0).astype(int)",
          "",
          "# Accidents without a bicycle: a stand-in for road traffic",
          "others = gpd.sjoin(acc_m[acc_m['IS_BICYCLE'] == 0][['geometry']], grid[['CELL_ID', 'geometry']], predicate='within')",
          "grid['OTHER_ACC'] = grid['CELL_ID'].map(others['CELL_ID'].value_counts()).fillna(0).astype(int)",
          "",
          "# Metres of cycling way inside each hexagon",
          "pieces = gpd.overlay(infra_m[['geometry']], grid[['CELL_ID', 'geometry']], how='intersection', keep_geom_type=True)",
          "grid['INFRA_M'] = grid['CELL_ID'].map(pieces.length.groupby(pieces['CELL_ID']).sum()).fillna(0).round(0)",
          "",
          "grid['INFRA_100M'] = grid['INFRA_M'] / 100",
          "grid['YOUNG_100']  = grid['YOUNG_ADULTS'] / 100",
          "z.show(grid[['BIKE_ACC', 'OTHER_ACC', 'INFRA_M', 'POPULATION', 'YOUNG_ADULTS']].describe().round(1).reset_index())"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "table",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Expected result",
          "Summary statistics of the five columns. The most important values:",
          "",
          "```",
          "              BIKE_ACC  OTHER_ACC  INFRA_M  POPULATION  YOUNG_ADULTS",
          "------------  --------  ---------  -------  ----------  ------------",
          "mean               1.7        2.5    153.1       196.5          29.4",
          "50% (median)         0          0        8          58             6",
          "max                 33         70     1703        1850           570",
          "```",
          "",
          "Most hexagons are quiet: half of them have no bicycle accident, no other accident and almost no cycling way. A few hexagons in the centre have very high values. The model has to explain both."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
