      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### OLS: one rule for the whole city",
          "",
          "**In one sentence:** OLS draws the \"best straight line\" through all hexagons: bicycle accidents = constant + a × other accidents + b × cycling way + c × young adults.",
          "",
          "**How it works:** it chooses the numbers a, b and c so that the squared differences between real and predicted accident counts are as small as possible. **R²** says which share of the differences between hexagons the model explains: 0 means nothing, 1 means everything.",
          "",
          "`OLSRegressor` gets the spatial weights from Part 5. It does not use them for the prediction, but it checks whether the model's errors are spatially clustered. If they are, a spatial model is the better choice."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": "Train the OLS model",
        "hasTitle": true,
        "message": [
          "%python",
          "",
          "FEATURES = ['OTHER_ACC', 'INFRA_100M', 'YOUNG_100']",
          "reg_sdf = SpatialDataFrame.create(GeoDataFrameDataset(grid[['BIKE_ACC'] + FEATURES + ['geometry']]))",
          "",
          "ols = SpatialPipeline([('regression', OLSRegressor(knn6))])",
          "ols.fit(reg_sdf, 'BIKE_ACC')",
          "print(ols.named_steps['regression'].summary)"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "raw",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "result": null,
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Expected result",
          "A summary of the model. The format of the summary is set by Spatial AI. Look for the coefficients:",
          "",
          "```",
          "Variable    Coefficient  Meaning",
          "----------  -----------  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
          "constant    about 0.0    a hexagon without traffic, cycling way or young residents has almost no bicycle accidents",
          "OTHER_ACC   about 0.36   each accident without a bicycle comes with about 0.36 bicycle accidents",
          "INFRA_100M  about 0.23   each 100 m of cycling way comes with about 0.23 bicycle accidents: where there are cycling ways, people cycle",
          "YOUNG_100   about 1.44   each 100 residents aged 18-29 come with about 1.4 bicycle accidents",
          "```",
          "",
          "All three effects are positive. The summary also contains spatial statistics of the errors, which the next paragraph shows in a simple form."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": true,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
